{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a powerful ruler who governed the County of Tripoli from 1146 to 1199. He is remembered as a significant figure in the Crusades and a skilled military leader. His reign marked a period of prosperity and expansion for the county though also faced considerable challenges.\n\n*Early Life and Ascension*\n\nRaymond was the son of Raymond I Count of Tripoli. He inherited the county upon his father's death in 1146. His early years were marked by consolidating power and dealing with internal rivalries. He successfully navigated the complex political landscape of the Levant establishing Tripoli as a major maritime power. He focused on strengthening the county’s defenses and fostering economic growth through trade. He also initiated important alliances with other influential figures in the region. Raymond’s leadership established a strong foundation for Tripoli’s future prominence.\n\n*Military Campaigns and Crusades*\n\nRaymond III was a prominent military leader participating in several Crusades. He fought alongside other Crusader lords in campaigns against Muslim forces in the Levant. He played a key role in the Third Crusade though his involvement was relatively minor compared to some other commanders. He demonstrated military prowess leading troops in battles and securing strategic territories. Raymond’s military successes significantly enhanced Tripoli’s prestige and influence. He built fortifications improved the county's defenses and expanded its control over coastal areas. He established a strong military force vital for defending Tripoli against external threats.\n\n*Legacy and Decline*\n\nRaymond III’s reign was characterized by both achievements and eventual decline. He fostered economic growth promoted trade and expanded the county’s territory. He left behind a well-defended and prosperous county. However his later years were marked by increasing internal strife and external pressures. The rise of powerful neighbors like the Ayyubid dynasty gradually eroded Tripoli’s power. He faced challenges from internal rebellions and external attacks leading to a gradual decline in the county’s authority. Despite his eventual downfall Raymond III is remembered as a successful and influential ruler who left a lasting mark on the history of the Crusader states and the Levant. His reign represents a significant period of stability and prosperity for Tripoli before its ultimate loss to the Ayyubids.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.16100043058395386}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -6.639736966462806e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.3841830625315197e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.08881326019763947}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.04918048158288002}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.5697049498558044}, {"token": "▁ruler", "logprob": -0.5181395411491394}, {"token": "▁who", "logprob": -0.5590880513191223}, {"token": "▁governed", "logprob": -1.4358240365982056}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.00026890001026913524}, {"token": "▁County", "logprob": -0.06798697263002396}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -1.4424220353248529e-05}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -0.35988783836364746}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.004324252251535654}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.00015877417172305286}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0005980133428238332}, {"token": "4", "logprob": -0.8045397400856018}, {"token": "6", "logprob": -0.33348581194877625}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.29744625091552734}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.0008248264202848077}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -1.1444026313256472e-05}, {"token": "9", "logprob": -0.009818356484174728}, {"token": "9", "logprob": -0.460307836532592